-- title:
--   Fixing the Δ-invariant field forces ρ(g)∈ρ(Δ)
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a_1,b_1$ and naturals $N,q,q'$ with $N$ nonzero and squarefree, $q$ and $q'$ prime, both at least $5$, $q'\neq q$, and neither dividing $N$. Assume $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and that for a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ every nonzero element of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a unit exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $R_1\le\Lambda_1$ be $\mathbb Z$-submodules of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ with $\Lambda_1$ a maximal order and $R_1$ an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$ in one of them; let $n_1$ be a finite-adelic unit lying in the Hecke set at $q$ for $R_1$ (that is, $n_1$ and $q\,n_1^{-1}$ lie in the finite adelic box of $R_1$ while $n_1^{-1}$ and $q^{-1}n_1$ do not), such that $S_1:=R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is again an intersection of two maximal orders, of relative index $Nq$, is stable under conjugation by $n_1$, and right translation by $n_1$ on the class set of the finite-idele stabiliser of $S_1$ is an involution; the class sets of the stabilisers of $S_1$ and of $R_1$ are assumed finite. Let $A_2$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A_2$, whose decomposition subgroup over $\mathbb Q$ acts isometrically for the valuation, let $v_2$ be a height-one prime containing $q$, let $K_0=\mathrm{ratClosure}\,A_2$ be the topological closure of the prime subfield in the completion $C$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for $A_2$, let $\iota_2:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$ be an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map and $\rho_2:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^\times\to\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ the induced projective representation, and let $\varpi_2$ be a pseudo-uniformizer of $K_0$ relative to $C$ (so $0<v(\varpi_2)<1$, with the scaling condition) whose image in $C$ is $q$; the ring $\mathrm{HolRingOf}\ \varpi_2\ \rho_2$ of functions on the upper half plane over $C$ that are holomorphic on each affinoid of the exhaustion attached to $\varpi_2$ is assumed to be a domain. Further data: for each prime $\ell\notin\{q,q'\}$ an element $s_2(\ell)\in\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^\times$ of reduced norm $\ell$ and a finite-adelic unit $sf_2(\ell)$ whose component at each place not containing $q$ is $s_2(\ell)\otimes 1$ and whose component at each place containing $q$ is $1$, such that the diagonal image of the scalar $\ell$ times $sf_2(\ell)^{-1}$ lies, when $\ell\mid N$, in the set of elements $h$ of the Hecke set at $\ell$ for $S_1$ with $hS_1h^{-1}\neq S_1$ and $S_1\not\le h\Lambda_1h^{-1}$, and otherwise in the Hecke set at $\ell$ for $S_1$. Let $\Gamma$ be the subgroup of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^\times$ consisting of the $x$ whose image at every height-one prime $w\neq v_2$ lies in the subgroup generated by the local box units of $R_1$ at $w$ and for which $\mathrm{ord}_q(\mathrm{nrd}\,x)$ is even, let $\Delta\le\Gamma$ be of nonzero relative index in $\Gamma$, and let $g\in\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^\times$ fix every element of the subfield of $\mathrm{Frac}(\mathrm{HolRingOf}\ \varpi_2\ \rho_2)$ fixed pointwise by $\Delta$. Then $\rho_2(g)$ lies in the image of $\Delta$ under $\rho_2$.
--
--   This is the faithfulness statement for the Mumford-curve description at the place over $q$: the $\Delta$-invariant subfield of the field of functions on Drinfeld's upper half plane determines $\Delta$ up to the kernel of the projective representation, so that only elements of $\rho_2(\Delta)$ fix it. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld descent, by [`CerednikDrinfeld.descentIntertwining_of_base_zero_one`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.descentIntertwining_of_base_zero_one) and by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_perm_quotVert_quotEdge_realisation_independent_of_descentIntertwining_zero_one`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_perm_quotVert_quotEdge_realisation_independent_of_descentIntertwining_zero_one), to identify Galois groups of the coverings built from the coset graph with the corresponding quaternionic groups.
